ACM Journal Article (acmart acmsmall) (typage/acm-journal) - license

This template contains files from two sources.

  main.tex, refs.bib, manifest.json, typage.json, LICENSE
      Written by 7D24H. CC0-1.0: dedicated to the public domain; documents
      written from this template need no attribution.
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

  acmart.cls, ACM-Reference-Format.bst
      The official ACM consolidated article template, acmart 2.20
      (2026/08/16), as distributed by CTAN and TeX Live
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/acmart; the archive https://mirrors.ctan.org/systems/texlive/tlnet/archive/acmart.tar.xz).
      acmart.cls is generated from acmart.dtx, which is under the LaTeX
      Project Public License 1.3c (Copyright the Association for Computing
      Machinery and Boris Veytsman). ACM-Reference-Format.bst is in the
      public domain, as stated in its header. Both files are redistributed
      unmodified, so that the template compiles offline.

The packages the class loads (Libertine fonts, natbib, hyperref, ...) come
from the built-in Tectonic bundle under their own licenses. Check
https://www.acm.org/publications/proceedings-template and your venue's call
for papers for the rules that apply to your submission.
